 '',
 '## Source model and authoritative documentation','',
 'A PubChem CID identifies a standardized Compound record; an SID identifies a depositor Substance submission. Several submissions may feed the same Compound and are not automatically independent evidence. CID identity is not the ontology’s canonical Substance identity. [NLM’s CID/SID explanation](https://support.nlm.nih.gov/knowledgebase/article/KA-03387/en-us) and the [Compound](https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/docs/compounds), [Substance](https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/docs/substances) and [data-source documentation](https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/docs/data-sources) establish these distinctions.',
 '',
